**Is anyone working on a ((Klingon)) translation?
***It's an interesting notion.  I wonder if Klingon possesses the semantic range necessary to talk about such things.  Perhaps a more interesting possibility would be a Lojban-only discussion of Lojban.  It's been called a turning point in a language's expressive power when it can describe itself.  And Lojban is much more completely expressive than Klingon. ''--mi'e ((Mark Shoulson|mark.))''
***.i mi tugni .i lo lojbo bangu velskicu be la lojban. cu cipra lejei la lojban. banzu lenu junri se pilno .i sa'enai lo bangu cu se pilno fi lenu bauskibau (toi zoigy. ''metalanguage'' gy.toi) cu cipra lejei cusku banzu -- mi'e nitcion noi li'a na ca nupre lenu fanva fi la lojban
*((Rapha묠Poss)) has a French [http://www.epita.fr/~poss_r/lojban/mythes.html|adaptation] of ((tsali))'s [http://people.fix.no/arj/lojban/myths.html|Myths About Lojban].
